You can add custom audio to your Minecraft map by following these steps:

1. Choose or create the audio you want to add to your map. This can be a sound effect, a music track, or a voiceover.
2. Convert the audio file to the appropriate format. Minecraft uses Ogg Vorbis format for audio files. You can use a program like Audacity to convert your audio file to Ogg Vorbis format.
3. Rename the audio file to the name you want to use in Minecraft. For example, if you want to add a custom music track to your map, name the file "music\_disc\_custom.ogg".
4. Place the audio file in the correct folder. For sounds, place the audio file in the "sounds" folder inside your Minecraft resource pack. For music, place the audio file in the "music" folder inside your Minecraft resource pack.
5. Create a sounds.json file. This file tells Minecraft where to find the audio file and how to play it. Here's an example of what the file might look like:
```json
{
  "custom.music": {
    "category": "music",
    "sounds": [
      {
        "name": "music_disc_custom",
        "stream": true
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
In this example, "custom.music" is the name you want to use for the audio in Minecraft. "music\_disc\_custom" is the name of the audio file you placed in the "music" folder. "stream" tells Minecraft to stream the audio instead of playing it all at once.

6. Save the sounds.json file in the "assets/minecraft/sounds" folder inside your Minecraft resource pack.
7. Load the resource pack in Minecraft and test the audio in your map.

By following these steps, you can add custom audio to your Minecraft map and create a more immersive experience for players.

You can make diamond armor change to a custom texture when you name it "hazmat" by following these steps:

1. Create the custom texture that you want to use for the hazmat armor. Make sure it is in the correct format, which is 64x64 pixels in PNG format.
2. Create a folder in your Minecraft resource pack and name it "assets/minecraft/models/item". This is where you will store the model file for the hazmat armor.
3. Create a new file in the "item" folder and name it "diamond\_helmet.json" (or whichever piece of diamond armor you want to modify). This file will tell Minecraft how to render the item.
4. Open the "diamond\_helmet.json" file in a text editor and add the following code:
```json
{
    "parent": "item/generated",
    "textures": {
        "layer0": "items/diamond_helmet"
    },
    "overrides": [
        {
            "predicate": {
                "custom_model_data": 1,
                "name": "hazmat"
            },
            "model": "item/hazmat_helmet"
        }
    ]
}
```
This code defines the model for the diamond helmet, and includes an "overrides" section that specifies a custom model to use when the helmet has a name of "hazmat" and has custom model data of 1.

5. Create a new file in the "item" folder and name it "hazmat\_helmet.json" (or whichever piece of diamond armor you want to modify). This file will define the custom model to use when the helmet has a name of "hazmat" and custom model data of 1.
6. Open the "hazmat\_helmet.json" file in a text editor and add the following code:
```json
{
    "parent": "item/generated",
    "textures": {
        "layer0": "items/hazmat_helmet"
    }
}
```
This code defines the model for the hazmat helmet, and specifies the custom texture to use.

7. Save both files and make sure they are in the correct location in your resource pack.
8. Load the resource pack in Minecraft and test the custom hazmat armor by renaming a diamond armor piece to "hazmat" and adding custom model data of 1.

By following these steps, you can create custom textured diamond armor that changes to a hazmat texture when it is named "hazmat".

