	* Checkout: Check out the source code from your GitHub repository.
	* Build: Install the dependencies for your project and run any necessary build steps.
	* Test: Run the unit tests for your project.
	* Deploy: Deploy the application to your production environment.
5. Configure your pipeline to trigger on code changes. You can set up a webhook in your GitHub repository to trigger your pipeline whenever code is pushed to the repository.
6. Test your pipeline by making changes to your code and pushing them to your GitHub repository.

