In PHP, you can use the Haversine formula to calculate the distance between two points on a sphere (such as the Earth) given their longitudes and latitudes. The Haversine formula is an equation that gives the distance between two points on a sphere based on their longitudes and latitudes.

Here is some sample code that demonstrates how to use the Haversine formula to calculate the distance between two points in PHP:
```
function haversineDistance($lat1, $lon1, $lat2, $lon2) {
    $earthRadius = 6371;
    $lat1 = deg2rad($lat1);
    $lon1 = deg2rad($lon1);
    $lat2 = deg2rad($lat2);
    $lon2 = deg2rad($lon2);
    $latDelta = $lat2 - $lat1;
    $lonDelta = $lon2 - $lon1;
    $angle = 2 * asin(sqrt(pow(sin($latDelta / 2), 2) +
        cos($lat1) * cos($lat2) * pow(sin($lonDelta / 2), 2)));
    return $angle * $earthRadius;
}

$distance = haversineDistance(38.4247341, -86.9624086, 43.0730517, -89.4012302);
echo $distance;
```
This code will output the distance in kilometers between the two points (38.4247341, -86.9624086) and (43.0730517, -89.4012302)

