Here is a simple Java program that compares the population densities of two countries:
```
import java.util.Scanner;

public class ComparePopulationDensities {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    // Create a Scanner object to read input from the user
    Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

    // Prompt the user to enter the name of the first country
    System.out.print("Enter the name of the first country: ");
    String country1 = scanner.nextLine();

    // Prompt the user to enter the population of the first country
    System.out.print("Enter the population of " + country1 + ": ");
    long population1 = scanner.nextLong();

    // Prompt the user to enter the area of the first country
    System.out.print("Enter the area of " + country1 + " in square kilometers: ");
    double area1 = scanner.nextDouble();

    // Prompt the user to enter the name of the second country
    System.out.print("Enter the name of the second country: ");
    String country2 = scanner.nextLine();

    // Prompt the user to enter the population of the second country
    System.out.print("Enter the population of " + country2 + ": ");
    long population2 = scanner.nextLong();

    // Prompt the user to enter the area of the second country
    System.out.print("Enter the area of " + country2 + " in square kilometers: ");
    double area2 = scanner.nextDouble();

    // Calculate the population density of the first country
    double density1 = population1 / area1;

    // Calculate the population density of the second country
    double density2 = population2 / area2;

    // Compare the population densities of the two countries
    if (density1 > density2) {
      System.out.println(country1 + " has a higher population density than " + country2);
    } else if (density1 < density2) {
      System.out.println(country2 + " has a higher population density than " + country1);
    } else {
      System.out.println(country1 + " and " + country2 + " have the same population density");
    }
  }
}
```
To use this program, you will need to enter the names of the two countries, their populations, and their areas in square kilometers. The program will then calculate the population densities of the two countries and compare them to determine which country has the higher population density.

To output all WordPress post titles and permalinks in an array, you can use the following function:
```php
function get_wordpress_posts() {
    $args = array(
        'post_type' => 'post',
        'post_status' => 'publish',
        'posts_per_page' => -1,
    );

    $posts_array = array();
    $query = new WP_Query( $args );

    if ( $query->have_posts() ) {
        while ( $query->have_posts() ) {
            $query->the_post();
            $post_title = get_the_title();
            $post_permalink = get_permalink();
            $posts_array[] = array(
                'title' => $post_title,
                'permalink' => $post_permalink,
            );
        }
    }

    wp_reset_postdata();

    return $posts_array;
}
```
This function uses the `WP_Query` class to retrieve all published posts and stores their titles and permalinks in an array. It then returns this array.

To use this function, you can simply call it in your WordPress code like this:
```php
$posts = get_wordpress_posts();

foreach ( $posts as $post ) {
    echo '<a href="' . $post['permalink'] . '">' . $post['title'] . '</a><br>';
}
```
This code will output all post titles as links with their corresponding permalinks.

